WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.969
To retire or not retire.

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:03.870
That is the question

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.071
still swarming around

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:06.740
Senator Dianne Feinstein.

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:08.041
The 89 year old California

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:10.010
Democrat is vowing to stay in office

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.044
through her term

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:12.979
despite being confined to a wheelchair

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:13.713
as she recovers

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:15.982
from a series of health issues.

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:17.917
The New York Times reporting since

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:18.818
returning to Washington,

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:20.353
Feinstein has missed six votes

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:22.122
and has not participated in any committee

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:24.290
hearings or caucus lunches.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:25.091
And The Washington Post

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:27.060
speaking to a divided California

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.062
Democratic delegates over the weekend.

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:30.630
This is from one from Rosemary Williams,

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:31.164
and she's

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:32.532
just following orders

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:34.467
as best she can at this point.

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:36.002
She's not herself.

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:37.670
Marcia Conant, on the other hand, said

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.439
it's extraordinary her career.

00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:41.408
And I think that's getting minimized

00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:43.676
and that makes me angry.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.178
Now, Feinstein,

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:46.546
the issues have been

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:47.480
happening for some time.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:48.882
She just suffered shingles

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:50.984
and related issues with it.

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:52.252
After she came back.

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:53.086
She didn't deny

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:55.021
she had broader health complications.

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:55.855
And then

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:56.456
she did have

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:58.091
broader health complications.

00:00:58.091 --> 00:01:00.026
As we reported on May 9th.

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:01.628
But she also had a memory issues

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:02.796
that she suffered for some time.

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:03.897
She was pushed aside

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:05.131
as the top Democrat

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:06.866
on the Senate Judiciary Committee.

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:08.301
She passed up being the president

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:09.235
pro tem,

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:10.437
which is for the most senior

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:12.472
member of the majority party.

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:13.640
Patty Murray now has that.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.208
So these are issues that have been

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:16.843
that she's been dealing with

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:17.644
for some time.

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:19.412
Can she sustained this?

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:22.515
So I think there are two things at play.

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:23.750
And unfortunately,

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.385
the politics is one of them.

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:26.920
And we can't ignore that.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.189
We can't ignore that.

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:30.190
She has a crew,

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:31.157
even though she's no longer

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:33.093
the top Democrat on Judiciary.

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:35.061
She's a crucial deciding vote

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:35.562
on that

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:37.230
very important committee,

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:39.399
especially in this divided government,

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:41.000
where so much of what

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.135
Democrats can accomplish

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:42.635
is focused

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:44.070
on confirming judges

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:46.473
and other Biden appointees.

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:50.577
So I think Democrats need Feinstein

00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:52.412
and there will create a lot of headaches

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:54.481
if she were to step down.

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:56.449
Governor Newsom doesn't want the headache

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:58.718
that would be created if she steps down.

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:01.387
And it also seems pretty clear that

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:02.856
whether you agree or not,

00:02:02.856 --> 00:02:04.190
she has decided

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.426
she does not want to step down.

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:08.094
But I think the other thing

00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:10.263
that a lot of people have brought up,

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:11.498
there's been some criticism

00:02:11.498 --> 00:02:12.365
that just

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:13.833
from a health standpoint,

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:16.302
from a wellness standpoint,

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:18.605
should the best thing for Senator

00:02:18.605 --> 00:02:21.541
Feinstein be to serve out,

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:24.544
to not serve out her term, instead

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:27.447
just kind of be able to go home and rest

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:28.515
and not have the stress

00:02:28.515 --> 00:02:29.582
of being in the U.S.

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:31.451
And it's been a staff ordeal,

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:33.052
as The New York Times reports.

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:34.220
They say that MS.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.688
Feinstein staff has made sure she is

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:37.257
never alone and is heavily protected.

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:38.224
The Capitol Police

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:39.492
and the Senate sergeant arms

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:41.060
have gone to great lengths to keep MS.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.228
Feinstein, shielded

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:43.897
from photographers and reporters,

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:45.865
helping to create a bubble around her

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:48.501
as aides run interference on her behalf.

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:49.836
I mean, I have personally experience

00:02:49.836 --> 00:02:50.303
that too.

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:51.838
I've tried to be in positions

00:02:51.838 --> 00:02:52.972
where we try to get video over.

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:54.407
They said that these are places

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:55.842
you're not allowed to get video of her.

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:56.543
They've tried

00:02:56.543 --> 00:02:57.277
intentionally trying

00:02:57.277 --> 00:02:59.145
to avoid press scrutiny.

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:00.547
Obviously, this is unusual

00:03:00.547 --> 00:03:01.614
given the access

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:02.916
we typically have on the Hill.

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:03.516
Absolutely.

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:04.651
That is extremely rare,

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:05.785
and it really does show

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:07.520
how Cognizant staff, I'm

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.722
sure her family, those around her

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:10.924
are about

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:12.425
just general press coverage

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:14.460
and how people are seeing her.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.863
I mean, it was a shock to so many people

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:18.765
when they opened the car door,

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:20.133
as you see right there.

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.901
And she arrived to the Senate

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.703
for the first time after months.

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:25.705
She just looked so frail.

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:27.106
The thing about the Senate, though,

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:29.042
and you have a really good point about,

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:29.209
you know,

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:29.742
the votes

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:32.579
and just needing to have someone there

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.814
tapping someone new would

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:35.748
possibly make it

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:36.449
a little difficult

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:37.984
in terms of timing of votes and,

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:40.353
you know, having all those people there.

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:41.588
But we've seen this time

00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:43.856
and time again with a number of senators.

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:44.190
You know,

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:45.892
this is not that rare

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:48.661
that many of them wish to be there

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:49.562
for, Kelly,

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:50.029
until the day

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:51.497
they get a perfect Segway

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:54.667
because this is indeed not an age old.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.102
It is an age old issue

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:57.670
to look at just a few headlines

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.073
from the past 2001,

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:01.808
a report about the 100 year

00:04:01.808 --> 00:04:02.375
old Strom

00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:04.244
Thurmond in the office, 2009

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:05.778
from someone named one a Roger,

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:07.614
a Politico pro Byrd illness,

00:04:07.614 --> 00:04:08.781
Cho's fragile majority.

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:10.016
She was my age as well.

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:11.918
And then also our industrious reporter,

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:13.086
Ted Barrett on Capitol

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:15.121
Hill in October 2017 about Thad Cochran

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:16.923
who ultimately resigned from office.

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:18.524
Robert Byrd was 92 after serving

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:19.592
51 years.

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:21.427
Nancy Pelosi says it's sexism

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:22.395
to go after Feinstein.

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:23.830
But this is really an issue

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:26.266
that's been happening for so many years.

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:27.367
It definitely has as long

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:28.701
as we've been covering the Hill.

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:31.471
The Strom Thurmond once you know

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:35.308
most particularly he could barely exist

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:36.542
he was living at Walter Reed,

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:37.543
if I recall,

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:38.478
and still serving the Senate.

00:04:38.478 --> 00:04:39.212
Look, the difference

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:41.247
here is the narrow majority

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:42.482
and the fact that she serves

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:43.416
on an important committee,

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:44.350
the Judiciary Committee

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:45.018
as you were saying.

00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:47.020
So I think that is what's at issue here.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:49.088
If she was simply on other committees

00:04:49.822 --> 00:04:50.957
or if it was another senator

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:51.424
whose vote

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:52.825
wasn't as critical

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:54.761
or if Democrats had more breathing room,

00:04:54.761 --> 00:04:56.095
we wouldn't be talking about this.

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:57.096
And it's politics.

00:04:57.096 --> 00:04:57.764
What is different?

00:04:57.764 --> 00:04:58.865
The politics in California

00:04:58.865 --> 00:04:59.766
is so fascinating

00:04:59.766 --> 00:05:00.600
because we have already

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:01.934
had a race to replace her

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:02.969
in a new somewhere

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:04.170
to just pick a replacement

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.239
and he has promised to pick a black woman

00:05:06.239 --> 00:05:07.240
while there is a black woman

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.975
in the race, probably.

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:10.143
And perhaps if he gave her

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:11.044
the replacement,

00:05:11.044 --> 00:05:12.612
could give a leg up against Adam Schiff,

00:05:12.612 --> 00:05:14.347
who Nancy Pelosi supports.

00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:15.581
Other supports.

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:16.182
Katie Porter

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:18.051
could give up a leg up against her.

00:05:18.051 --> 00:05:19.252
Who knows if he'd pick Barbara Lee.

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:19.886
But still,

00:05:19.886 --> 00:05:21.721
there are politics at play here, right?

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:22.622
Because regardless,

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:24.223
he said he'll pick a black woman,

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:25.758
which even if it's not Barbara

00:05:25.758 --> 00:05:26.859
Lee, and quite frankly,

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:28.194
it would be hard for him to pick

00:05:28.194 --> 00:05:29.162
Barbara Lee,

00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:30.830
given the fact that Adam Schiff

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:33.599
and Katie Porter are also in the race in

00:05:33.866 --> 00:05:35.835
Nobody wants to have that perception

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:36.903
as putting their thumb

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:37.637
on the scale of such

00:05:37.637 --> 00:05:40.139
an important Senate seat for Democrats.

00:05:40.907 --> 00:05:42.742
But then if it's not Barbara Lee,

00:05:42.742 --> 00:05:44.110
then it becomes well, who is it?

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:45.745
And then that creates a whole nother

00:05:45.745 --> 00:05:47.880
discussion in California.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:48.848
So, again,

00:05:48.848 --> 00:05:50.383
I think Governor Newsom would

00:05:50.383 --> 00:05:52.785
rather not have that on his plate.

00:05:53.586 --> 00:05:55.988
But that means that Senator Feinstein

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:59.025
remains in office through 20, 24.

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:00.560
We'll see if the Senate comes back

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:02.428
this week. We'll see what happens then.

